{"book":13,"chapter":31,"rubric":"PYTHON AS A FIRST LANGUAGE / METAPROGRAMMING / CHAPTER 31","slides":[{"title":"Class is an object too","sub":"The type chain","short":"Class is an object","main":"type is the class of classes, and it closes on itself.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Value and class","Class of a class","type closes on itself"],"captions":["3 is an instance of int; the class int is an object too, with a class of its own","type(int) is type: the \"class of classes\", the thing that creates classes","type(type) is type too: the chain closes on itself, and all classes end up inheriting object"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":14.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"int","tone":"green","size":14.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":128.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":168.0,"y":56.0,"text":"type(3)","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":56.0,"y":70.0,"w":56.0,"h":30.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":160.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"int","tone":"green","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"type","tone":"yellow","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":86.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":122.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":198.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"int","tone":"green","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":56.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"type","tone":"yellow","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":190.0,"y":112.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"object","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":108.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":154.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":190.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":98.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":300.0,"y":56.0,"text":"type(type)\n→ type","tone":"yellow","size":10.0}]],"cues":[13.9,31.5]}]},{"title":"type with three arguments","sub":"class = a call to type","short":"type(...)","main":"The class statement is a handy way to write type(name, bases, dict).","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Plain class","type(...)","The same thing"],"captions":["The class statement is shorthand","type(name, bases, dict) creates the same class with a function call","The result is the same class: both variants give Point with a hello method"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Point:","    def hello(self):","        return 'hi'"],"lang":"python","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":230.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def hello(self):","    return 'hi'","","Point = type('Point', (), {'hello': hello})"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"class Point","tone":"blue","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"type('Point', …)","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"text":"=","tone":"yellow","size":22.0}]],"cues":[13.4,22.2]}]},{"title":"Dynamic classes","sub":"Class from a description","short":"Dynamics","main":"Dynamic classes are invisible to editors.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Field description","Assembly","Finished class"],"captions":["A list of fields was read from a file — we want a class with those fields that can print itself","Build a dict of methods and call type(...)","The class is no different from a handwritten one; this is how namedtuple and similar tools work"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["fields = ['x', 'y', 'z']","# from a file or a schema"],"lang":"python","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":220.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["def make(name, fields):","    def init(self, *vals):","        self.__dict__.update(zip(fields, vals))","    return type(name, (), {'__init__': init})"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["P = make('P', ['x', 'y'])","p = P(1, 2)","p.x + p.y     # 3"],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":26.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"an editor won't see such a class","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}]],"cues":[11.4,25.4]}]},{"title":"Five steps","sub":"What class does","short":"Five steps","main":"Metaclass, namespace, body, creation, hooks.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Metaclass","Namespace","Body","Creation","Hooks"],"captions":["Parents and the metaclass are determined — the thing that will create the class","__prepare__ prepares the namespace for the body — usually an empty dict","The class body runs as ordinary code, all definitions land in the namespace","The metaclass(name, bases, namespace) is called and returns the finished class","__set_name__ is called on descriptors, __init_subclass__ on the parent"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1. parents and metaclass","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2. __prepare__ → namespace","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":82.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3. class body runs","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"4. metaclass(name, bases, ns)","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":138.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"5. __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1. parents and metaclass","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2. __prepare__ → namespace","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":82.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3. class body runs","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"4. metaclass(name, bases, ns)","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":138.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"5. __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1. parents and metaclass","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2. __prepare__ → namespace","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":82.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3. class body runs","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"4. metaclass(name, bases, ns)","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":138.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"5. __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1. parents and metaclass","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2. __prepare__ → namespace","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":82.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3. class body runs","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"4. metaclass(name, bases, ns)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":138.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"5. __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1. parents and metaclass","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2. __prepare__ → namespace","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":82.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3. class body runs","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"4. metaclass(name, bases, ns)","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":138.0,"w":250.0,"h":22.0,"text":"5. __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.2,19.0,26.1,33.6]}]},{"title":"Your own metaclass","sub":"Inherit type","short":"Metaclass","main":"A metaclass is inherited by descendants.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Inherit type","Using it","Inherited"],"captions":["A metaclass is a class whose instances are classes; inherit type and override __new__","Plugged in by a keyword argument: class A(metaclass=Meta)","A metaclass is inherited: all descendants are created by the same metaclass; incompatible metaclasses conflict"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["class Meta(type):","    def __new__(mcs, name, bases, ns):","        ns['created_by'] = 'Meta'","        return super().__new__(mcs, name, bases, ns)"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class A(metaclass=Meta):","    pass","A.created_by   # 'Meta'"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Meta","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":90.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"A","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":90.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"B(A)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":44.0,"x2":112.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":44.0,"x2":248.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":226.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[20.0,26.6]}]},{"title":"What they are for","sub":"Enum, ABC, ORM","short":"Why","main":"Ninety-nine in a hundred do without metaclasses.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["99 in 100 don't need it","Enum and ABC","Models"],"captions":["The language authors: ninety-nine percent of programmers don't need metaclasses","But enumerations (member order, no reassignment) and abstract classes (no instantiation) stand on them","An ORM builds a table schema from class fields — at creation time, so errors show at once"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":220.0,"h":40.0,"text":"99 in 100","tone":"yellow","size":20.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"do without metaclasses","size":10.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"EnumMeta","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"ABCMeta","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"text":"members in order","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"text":"can't create without methods","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class User(Model):","    name = TextField()","    age = IntField()","# → CREATE TABLE user (...)"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[12.1,28.0]}]},{"title":"Metaclass in action","sub":"Collecting commands","short":"In action","main":"A metaclass can change the namespace.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Namespace","Pick cmd_","Command table"],"captions":["The metaclass gets the namespace before the class exists — it can not only read it but change it","Pick functions with the cmd_ prefix and store them by short name","Any class with this metaclass gets a commands table with no extra code from the author"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":46.0,"lines":["ns = {","  'cmd_add': <func>,","  'cmd_del': <func>,","  'helper':  <func>,","}"],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":260.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":46.0,"lines":["ns = {","  'cmd_add': <func>,","  'cmd_del': <func>,","  'helper':  <func>,","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":260.0},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"cmd_ ?","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["ns['commands'] = {","  'add': <func>,","  'del': <func>,","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":260.0}]],"cues":[6.8,28.5]}]},{"title":"Metaclass __call__","sub":"Creating instances","short":"call","main":"Order: __call__, __new__, __init__.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Calling a class","Order","Singleton"],"captions":["A() actually triggers __call__ of the metaclass","It calls the class's __new__, then its __init__","Override __call__ — and you can return the same instance, keep count, or cache by arguments"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"A()","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Meta.__call__(A)","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":112.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":164.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Meta.__call__","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":28.0,"text":"A.__new__","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":28.0,"text":"A.__init__","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":228.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":260.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["class Singleton(type):","    _inst = {}","    def __call__(cls, *a, **kw):","        if cls not in cls._inst:","            cls._inst[cls] = super().__call__(*a, **kw)","        return cls._inst[cls]"],"hl":[3,4,5],"lang":"python","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.5,28.4]}]},{"title":"__init_subclass__","sub":"Subclass hook","short":"Hook","main":"A hook is usually enough instead of a metaclass.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Hook","Arguments","Simpler than a metaclass"],"captions":["__init_subclass__ is a class method called on the parent when each descendant is defined","Keyword arguments after the parents arrive in it: class Json(Base, name='json')","No new metaclass and no conflicts — if a hook is enough, use the hook"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class Base:","    def __init_subclass__(cls, **kw):","        super().__init_subclass__(**kw)","        print('new subclass', cls.__name__)"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def __init_subclass__(cls, name=None, **kw):","    super().__init_subclass__(**kw)","    key = name or cls.__name__.lower()","    registry[key] = cls","","class Json(Base, name='json'): ..."],"hl":[0,5],"lang":"python","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"__init_subclass__","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"metaclass","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"a hook is usually enough","tone":"green","size":10.0}]],"cues":[15.8,28.0]}]},{"title":"Registry","sub":"Plugins","short":"Registry","main":"Descendants join the registry automatically.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Base class","Descendants","Pick by string"],"captions":["The base class keeps a registry dict — it is empty","Each descendant gets in automatically: the name from an argument or from the class name","The program picks an implementation by a settings string: registry['json']() — required-attribute checks go there too"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Base","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"registry = { }","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Base","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Json","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":170.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Csv","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":56.0,"text":"'json' → Json\n'csv' → Csv","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":86.0,"y1":52.0,"x2":76.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":120.0,"y1":52.0,"x2":164.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":224.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":232.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["fmt = settings['format']   # 'json'","reader = registry[fmt]()"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":28.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[12.4,22.2]}]},{"title":"Other hooks","sub":"__class_getitem__, __prepare__","short":"Other hooks","main":"Class creation is open to customization.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__class_getitem__","__prepare__","Openness"],"captions":["Box[int] calls __class_getitem__ on the class itself — that is how list[int] gets a generic alias","__prepare__ lets you slip in your own namespace: for example, forbid duplicate method names","Class creation is fully open to customization, not hidden inside the interpreter"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["Box[int]","# → Box.__class_getitem__(int)","# → types.GenericAlias(Box, (int,))"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["class NoDup(dict):","    def __setitem__(self, k, v):","        if k in self:","            raise TypeError(k)","        super().__setitem__(k, v)"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":200.0,"h":34.0,"text":"class creation","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"open to customization","tone":"yellow","size":11.0}]],"cues":[12.7,24.5]}]},{"title":"Traps","sub":"Careful","short":"Traps","main":"Decorator, descriptor or hook first.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Readability","Metaclass conflict","Overkill"],"captions":["Metaclasses are hard to read and debug, and editors and type checkers often don't understand them","With multiple inheritance metaclasses may conflict — a common metaclass subclass is needed","Most often a metaclass is used where a class decorator, a descriptor or __init_subclass__ would do"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"metaclass","tone":"red","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"text":"?!","tone":"red","size":28.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"MetaA","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":56.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"MetaB","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":130.0,"y":112.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"class C(A, B)","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":82.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":118.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":178.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":142.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":300.0,"y":112.0,"text":"TypeError","tone":"red","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"decorator","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"descriptor","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"hook","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"try them first","size":10.5}]],"cues":[16.0,27.5]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Metaclasses","short":"Summary","main":"Choose the simplest tool.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["type","Class creation","Metaclass","Choosing a tool"],"captions":["A class is an object, created by type; type(name, bases, dict) can be called directly","class: body, metaclass, then __set_name__ and __init_subclass__","A metaclass inherits type: __new__ controls class creation, __call__ — instance creation","Decorator, descriptor, __init_subclass__ hook first — and only then a metaclass"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"int","tone":"green","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"type","tone":"yellow","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":142.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":198.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"body","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"metaclass","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"hooks","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":70.0,"ton